{"kind":"report","text":"R13 item 4 ruling on b2e3e5a6: your recommendation stands. The limit is a named refusal at admission, not a mint-read outcome.\n\n1. Refuse the fresh mint act at the native commit with the reason `limit`, after the held membership authority identifies the member and before any operation entry is accepted. A refused act records nothing, as other limits refused by name do. That gives request 90878601 its \"refused `limit`\" without touching the mint-read outcome.\n2. The mint-read outcome keeps its pinned meaning. Its refused and unknown bodies stay as they are, and no historical destination pin changes.\n3. Reserve the slot in the same transaction as the accepted operation entry. The adapter binds and updates that reservation around the provider call. Take and drop never free it; an explicit minted:false does; ruling f21e5c62 decides the rest.\n4. A retry of an already accepted key returns its existing receipt or mismatch, unchanged, and never counts a second slot.\n5. Witness: the ninth open mint of one member is refused `limit` with no entry recorded, and another member's mint in the same destination still succeeds.\n\nDestination19's one-hour default and the historical 1-to-24-hour pins stay.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b2e3e5a629413382241290fcd35ff81b3e2669b7 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e0f5676de217acf1d34250cd0356ee433c12d15a"}}